score_rev_durability":58.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.24270413653909206,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.002061683752043504,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":52.1,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05509936096049599,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":72.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.004045414868772079,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":44.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0011296371605440333,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.027709998,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":18.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Plains GP Holdings, L.P., through its subsidiary, Plains All American Pipeline, L.P., owns and operates midstream infrastructure systems in the United States and Canada. It operates through Crude Oil and Natural Gas Liquids (NGLs) segments. The company engages in the gathering and transporting crude oil using pipelines, trucks, and barges or railcars. It also provides terminalling, storage, and other related services. In addition, the company is involved in the natural gas processing and NGL fractionation, storage, transportation, and terminalling activities. PAA GP Holdings LLC operates as a general partner of the company. Plains GP Holdings, L.P. was incorporated in 2013 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Wilfred C.W. Chiang | Chairman, President & CEO of PAA GP Holdings LLC | Age 64 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Plains GP Holdings, L.P. is a mid-cap energy business with a $6.1B market cap on $44.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Gross margins of 5% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $2.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 11.27\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio of 456% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 40% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4047892170920562},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Energy peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 82% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (PAGP) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/81/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_PAGP_Edition_111226103202_1794540722.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794540722.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Plains GP Holdings (PAGP) Just Gave Investors Something To Think About","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nasdaq-pagp/plains-gp-holdings/news/plains-gp-holdings-pagp-just-gave-investors-something-to-thi","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794529780.098,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.923,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Will Mixed Quarter Earnings Change Plains GP Holdings (PAGP) Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nasdaq-pagp/plains-gp-holdings/news/will-mixed-quarter-earnings-change-plains-gp-holdings-pagp-n","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794440740.412,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.052,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Plains GP (NYSE:PAGP) and Murphy Oil (NYSE:MUR) Head to Head Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/plains-gp-nysepagp-and-murphy-oil-nysemur-head-to-head-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794401125.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.94,"tier":0,"sco